& [SJS]
  + Situation: provider-free capabilities are verified but distributed across modules artifacts solutions and proofs
  + Justification: one regenerated digest index supplies a machine-readable table of contents without copying the indexed bodies
  + Solution: commit each major fixture output in dependency order and publish one root plus an explicit true-false capability ledger

& [Delineation]
  + artifact commitment proves exact deterministic generated bytes and not provider provenance
  + capability true is restricted to verified provider-free form behavior
  + capability false preserves live and effectful boundaries rather than implying future impossibility
  + root digest is a content commitment and not a producer signature or authorization

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + artifact kind enum fixes the finite index vocabulary
  + ordinal and kind together fix dependency order
  + each commitment retains profile byte count and domain-separated content digest
  + root commits only the compact commitment list so large artifact bodies remain outside the index

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty prevents generated fixture identity from inflating into physical execution
  + Security validates each upstream artifact before commitment and keeps denied capabilities false
  + Planner fixes dependency order and complete expected membership
  + Weaver joins independent outputs under one root without merging their identities
  + Scribe creates an inspectable machine-readable table of contents
  + Refiner retains digests and byte counts instead of repeating full artifacts
  + Observer regenerates all upstream outputs and the root before accepting the index

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated lineage_index forms generator validator serializer CLI artifact and adversarial tests
  + keep live provider persistence hidden state effects remote execution and Minecraft outside authority

& [Rollback]
  + additive module CLI branch artifact exports and tests remove without changing predecessor behavior
